# Security Rules

- Validate all external input server-side.
- Enforce authorization server-side; UI hiding is not authorization.
- Use secure authentication/session handling.
- Protect against injection, XSS, CSRF where applicable, broken access control, and unsafe redirects.
- Rate-limit authentication, OTP, password reset, sensitive forms, and abuse-prone endpoints.
- Never expose stack traces or internal errors to users.
- Never log passwords, tokens, card data, CVV, secrets, or unnecessary sensitive customer data.
- Keep secrets server-side and out of source control.
- Validate file uploads by type, size, extension, and storage policy.
- Use secure cookies where applicable.
- Add and test appropriate security headers in production.
- Maintain audit logs for sensitive administrative actions.
- Treat security findings as higher priority than cosmetic improvements.
